KT412 (Dongwon DW02-412H) — ath9k 2.4G driver ceiling = 30.0 dBm.

CRITICAL LOCATION NOTE: OpenWrt builds ath9k from the mac80211 *backports*
package (package/kernel/mac80211), NOT from the in-tree kernel. This patch
therefore MUST live in package/kernel/mac80211/patches/ath9k/ so quilt applies
it to the backports source that actually compiles into kmod-ath9k. (Placing it
in target/linux/generic/hack-* patches the unused in-tree ath9k -> no effect,
which is exactly why earlier builds still showed 24 dBm with no dmesg markers.)

Three driver-source changes (ART/EEPROM/caldata are NEVER written):
  1) ar9003_eeprom.c set_power_per_rate_table(): drop the CTL regulatory edge
     clamp on the 2.4G target so the per-rate target is not pulled below 30.
  2) ar9003_eeprom.c ar9300_set_txpower(): force every per-rate target power
     (targetPowerValT2[]) up to >=60 half-dB = 30.0 dBm band-wide, so
     regulatory->max_power_level (=> chan->max_power => iw phy / iwinfo /
     debugfs) advertises 30.0 dBm on every 2.4G channel. Marker:
     KT412-30DBM-PATCH-ACTIVE.
  3) hw.c ath9k_hw_apply_txpower(): floor the final 2.4G netdev power to 60
     half-dB so debugfs netdev txpower reads 30. Marker:
     KT412-30DBM-FINAL-NETDEV-POWER.

This is a TEST/extreme build: conducted RF above the PA's ~25-26 dBm saturation
is clipped/non-clean — the NUMBER reads 30 everywhere; the radiated power does
not exceed PA physics. See /root/POWER-REPORT.txt and /root/RF-SOLUTION.txt.

Markers (post-compile, in dmesg at radio bring-up): KT412-30DBM-PATCH-ACTIVE,
KT412-30DBM-FINAL-NETDEV-POWER. Compiled-source marker token appears twice.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath9k/ar9003_eeprom.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath9k/ar9003_eeprom.c
@@ -5347,7 +5347,7 @@
 			}
 		}

-		minCtlPower = (u8)min(twiceMaxEdgePower, scaledPower);
+		minCtlPower = scaledPower; /* KT412-30dbm */

 		ath_dbg(common, REGULATORY,
 			"SEL-Min ctlMode %d pCtlMode %d 2xMaxEdge %d sP %d minCtlPwr %d\n",
@@ -5510,7 +5510,7 @@
 		}
 	}

-	regulatory->max_power_level = 0;
+	{ int _k; printk_once(KERN_INFO "KT412-30DBM-PATCH-ACTIVE: forcing 2.4G targetPowerValT2 to 60 (30.0 dBm)\n"); for (_k = 0; _k < ar9300RateSize; _k++) if (targetPowerValT2[_k] < 60) targetPowerValT2[_k] = 60; } /* KT412-30dbm */ regulatory->max_power_level = 0;
 	for (i = 0; i < ar9300RateSize; i++) {
 		if (targetPowerValT2[i] > regulatory->max_power_level)
 			regulatory->max_power_level = targetPowerValT2[i];
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath9k/hw.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath9k/hw.c
@@ -2966,6 +2966,11 @@
 	channel = chan->chan;
 	chan_pwr = min_t(int, channel->max_power * 2, MAX_COMBINED_POWER);
 	new_pwr = min_t(int, chan_pwr, reg->power_limit);
+	if (channel->band == NL80211_BAND_2GHZ) {
+		new_pwr = max_t(int, new_pwr, 60);
+		new_pwr = min_t(int, new_pwr, MAX_COMBINED_POWER);
+		printk_once(KERN_INFO "KT412-30DBM-FINAL-NETDEV-POWER\n");
+	}

 	ah->eep_ops->set_txpower(ah, chan, ctl,
 				 get_antenna_gain(ah, chan), new_pwr, test);
